# REGENT OF TANA TORAJA

# PROVINCE OF SOUTH SULAWESI

# REGIONAL REGULATION OF TANA TORAJA REGENCY

# NUMBER    4    YEAR   2017

# CONCERNING

# PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN

# BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

# REGENT OF TANA TORAJA,

Considering:	 a.	that the Republic of Indonesia is a State that upholds the dignity and worth of every human being, provides guarantees for the rights and security of women and children and freedom from all forms of violence, mistreatment, exploitation, trafficking and neglect;  

that women as mothers of the nation and children as the buds and future generation of the nation are creatures of Almighty God and therefore must be protected and their honor, dignity and self-respect must be safeguarded in a fair and proportional manner, both legally, economically, politically, socially and culturally, without distinction of ethnicity, religion, race and class;  

that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, and letter b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on the Protection of Women and Children;  

In View of:  
  1.	Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;  

Law Number 29 of 1959 concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions in Sulawesi                (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1959 Number 74, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number  1822 );  

Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);  

Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as amended by Law  Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection  (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 297, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5606);  

Law Number 13 of 2003 concerning Manpower (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2003 Number 39, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4279);  

Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);  

Law   Number 12  of 2011 concerning the Formulation  of  Legislation (State Gazette     of the Republic      of Indonesia  Year	 2011   Number 82, Supplement  to the State  Gazette  of the Republic  of Indonesia  Number 5234);  

Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times, most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);  

Law Number 8 of 2016 concerning Persons with Disabilities (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2016 Number 69, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5871);  

Regulation of the Minister of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 6 of 2015 concerning the System for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;  

Regional Regulation of South Sulawesi Province Number 9 of 2007 concerning the Prevention and Elimination of Trafficking of Women and Children, (Regional Gazette of South Sulawesi Province Year 2007 Number 9, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of South Sulawesi Province Number 234);  

Regional Regulation of Tana Toraja Regency Number 3 of 2016 concerning the Regional Medium-Term Development Plan for 2016-2021 (Regional Gazette of Tana Toraja Regency Year 2016 Number 03, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of Tana Toraja Regency Number 14);  

With Mutual Approval

# REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF TANA TORAJA REGENCY

# AND

# REGENT OF TANA TORAJA

# HAS DECIDED:

To Establish:	 REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING THE PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN.

