#### Article 4

The implementation of child protection is based on Pancasila and the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia as well as the basic principles of the convention on the rights of the child including: non-discrimination;

the best interests of the child;

the right to life, survival, and development; and respect for the views of the child.

#### Article 5

The objectives of implementing protection for women are: to ensure the fulfillment of women's rights;

to protect and provide a sense of security for women;

to maintain household integrity in order to realize a harmonious and prosperous family;

to ensure the fulfillment of women's rights;

to provide services to women;

to provide protection to reporters and witnesses; and to empower women victims of violence.

#### Article 6

The objectives of implementing child protection are: to ensure the fulfillment of children's rights;

to protect and provide a sense of security for children;

to maintain household integrity in order to realize a harmonious and prosperous family;

to ensure the fulfillment of children's rights;

to realize quality children with noble character and prosperity;

to provide services to child victims of violence; and to provide protection to reporters and witnesses.

# CHAPTER IV

## IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN

## Part One

Rights of Women

#### Article 7

The rights of women are as follows: to live, maintain life and improve their standard of living;

to live peacefully, safely, in peace, happily, prosperously both physically and spiritually;

to enjoy a good and healthy living environment;

to live in a family and continue offspring in a legal marriage bond based on the provisions of laws and regulations;

to obtain work according to ability, conditions and fair and just wages;

specifically for women with disabilities, the right to obtain facilities and special treatment in public services;

to play an active role in the political and governmental fields in accordance with their potential and capabilities;

to obtain information and legal services;

to obtain services to increase their income; and to obtain other rights in accordance with their human dignity and based on the provisions of laws and regulations.

## Part Two

Empowerment of Women

#### Article 8

In order to improve the position, role, and quality of women, as well as efforts to realize gender equality and justice in family life, community life, national life, and state life, women must be empowered.

The empowerment of women as referred to in paragraph (1) is directed to obtain opportunities and their rights as human beings, so that they are able to play a role and participate in activities of: economy;

social culture;

politics; and law.

#### Article 9

The implementation of women's empowerment in the economic field as referred to in Article 8 paragraph (2) letter a, is carried out through: provision of skills and job training;

facilitation of the formation of productive economic business groups;

facilitation of strengthening and development of productive economic business groups;

facilitation of capital assistance; and facilitation of marketing network development.

#### Article 10

Women's empowerment in the social and cultural field as referred to in Article 8 paragraph (2) letter b, is carried out through: improvement of knowledge, attitudes and skills to encourage the fulfillment of education in stages according to potential to improve social status;

improvement of awareness, willingness and ability to overcome health problems through quality promotive, preventive, curative, and rehabilitative efforts, especially in the field of reproductive health;

improvement of awareness and knowledge about independent, healthy and prosperous family planning including access to consultation services and marriage registration; and
d. facilitation and efforts to preserve customs and the development of science, technology, arts and culture for the advancement of women.

#### Article 11

The implementation of women's empowerment in the political field as referred to in Article 8 paragraph (2) letter c, includes: involvement of women in decision-making at various levels;

provision of opportunities for women to hold public office;

participation in general elections; and self-development through organizations to associate, assemble and express opinions.

The implementation of women's empowerment in the political field as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

#### Article 12

The implementation of women's empowerment in the legal field as referred to in Article 8 paragraph (2) letter d, includes: improvement of awareness and knowledge in the legal field through communication, information and education services; and facilitation of access and legal consultation services.

The implementation of women's empowerment in the legal field as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

#### Article 13

The Regional Government has the obligation and responsibility in efforts to empower women.

The efforts to empower women as referred to in paragraph (1) are carried out in an integrated manner in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

